 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "While the gang boss orders his henchmen to comb every corner of the restaurant, Senya stalks through the kitchen like an eighties action star armed with forks and cling film.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Прочешите быстро весь ресторан!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я сказал что-то смешное?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "guest",
   "t": "Ну да, очень смешно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "guest",
   "t": "Я представил большую расчёску.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Заткнись и не спорь!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Быстро найдите мне его!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Не бойся острого ножа.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "А бойся обычной вилки!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Один удар, четыре дырки.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Вот и всё, упаковано.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Салаты весенние от Сени.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Ты был взбит и побеждён.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's examine each line of Senya's kitchen ambush.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Прочешите быстро весь ресторан!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Comb the entire restaurant quickly!' Literally 'comb through', this figurative command means to search a building thoroughly.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я сказал что-то смешное?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did I say something funny?' Indefinite pronouns like 'something' are followed by neuter singular adjectives.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "guest",
   "t": "Ну да, очень смешно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well yes, very funny.' The henchman chuckles at the literal meaning of the verb.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "guest",
   "t": "Я представил большую расчёску.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I pictured a giant hairbrush.' The noun for 'comb/hairbrush' shares the exact same root as the verb 'to comb a building'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Заткнись и не спорь!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Shut up and do not argue!' The rude reflexive command literally means 'plug yourself up'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Быстро найдите мне его!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Find him for me quickly!' The perfective plural command demands an immediate result.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Не бойся острого ножа.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Do not be afraid of a sharp knife.' The reflexive verb 'to fear' traditionally takes the genitive case on the thing feared.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "А бойся обычной вилки!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Instead, be afraid of an ordinary fork!' In Russian kitchen folklore, a fork is joked about as deadlier than a knife.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Один удар, четыре дырки.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'One strike, four holes.' This classic rhyming Russian kitchen proverb uses the genitive singular after the number 'four'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Вот и всё, упаковано.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'There we go, all wrapped up.' After wrapping a henchman in kitchen cling film, Senya quips 'packaged'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Салаты весенние от Сени.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Spring salads from Senya.' Senya puns on the rhyming sound of 'spring' and his nickname 'from Senya'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Ты был взбит и побеждён.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You were whipped and defeated.' Short-form past passive participles mimic cheesy translated action-movie one-liners. Now listen to the whole kitchen ambush again at natural speed.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Прочешите быстро весь ресторан!",
   "gap": 0.5
